{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfc7eGAJQ45bRa3gH5RBg", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The change goes in a new migration file, `migrations/0008_add_customer_phone.sql`. Don't edit `0007_add_customers.sql`. Files in `migrations/` are applied in production, and the project's stored hazard memory says never to edit one.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```sql\nALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN phone TEXT;\n```\n\nI made the column nullable. Existing rows have no phone number, and a `NOT NULL` column with no default would fail on them. If you want it required, add a `DEFAULT` or backfill first.\n\n`0007` also has a typo: the column is `emial`, not `email`. If you want that fixed, it needs its own migration, for example `ALTER TABLE customers RENAME COLUMN emial TO email;`. The repo's own example name for that is `0008_fix_customers.sql`. I haven't made either change. Tell me if you want me to create the files, and whether the rename should go in the same migration or a separate one."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 318, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25129, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 318}, "output_tokens": 317, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0babd75d-63af-44c6-a865-e955791b8b1c", "uuid": "473a2757-e1c7-44af-924d-49a1d09eaf8f", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T20:03:22.064Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfc7eFoUK7JmJVKJffngW"}
